CodeBrix patch 0007 - non-aborting wgpuDevicePoll / wgpuInstanceProcessEvents (wgpu-native/src/lib.rs)

WHAT: a failed wgpuDevicePoll wait (a submission index this device's queue never returned, a device
error) returns WGPUBool false and reports through the device's own error path (handle_error: error
scopes / uncaptured-error callback; DeviceError::Lost reaches the device-lost callback) instead of
handle_error_fatal (a panic = process abort at the C boundary). WaitIdleError::Timeout (unreachable
today - no timeout is passed) returns false without an error. wgpuInstanceProcessEvents (void, no
device to report to) logs the failure (log::error!) instead of aborting. The Rust signature now
uses native::WGPUBool for `wait` and the result, as wgpu.h declares (it used Rust's one-byte bool:
a C caller reading the WGPUBool result saw garbage in the upper 24 bits - observed 0xFFFFFF01 for
"true" on x86_64). The C signature (wgpu.h) is unchanged.
WHY: a C caller - and Rust catch_unwind above it - cannot survive an abort; a bounded poll needs a
poll that can fail.
UPSTREAM: no fix exists for the abort. Trunk (589e6caa4e) and open PR #630 both still call
handle_error_fatal in both functions. PR #630 also moves wgpuDevicePoll to WGPUBool parameters, but
together with a C signature change (timeout, WGPUNativePollStatus) not taken here. CodeBrix's own
change.

--- a/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
+++ b/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
@@ -2955,8 +2955,11 @@ pub unsafe extern "C" fn wgpuInstanceProcessEvents(instance: native::WGPUInstanc
 
     match context.poll_all_devices(false) {
         Ok(_queue_empty) => (),
+        // CodeBrix (patches/0007): logged instead of aborting the process. The instance has no
+        // per-device error sink to route it to; the failing device reports the same failure on
+        // its own path at its next wgpuDevicePoll or use.
         Err(cause) => {
-            handle_error_fatal(cause, "wgpuInstanceProcessEvents");
+            log::error!("wgpuInstanceProcessEvents: {}", format_error(&cause));
         }
     }
 }
